WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.060
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.330 --> 00:07.240
- [Previously…] - If you’re really set on leaving,

3
00:07.570 --> 00:09.000
I’ll let you take the exam in Bangkok.

4
00:09.213 --> 00:11.360
And stop thinking I’m so mean.

5
00:11.576 --> 00:13.100
I love you more than anyone in this family, dumbass.

6
00:13.677 --> 00:14.720
You can't leave me, okay?

7
00:16.414 --> 00:18.123
- Promise? - Promise.

8
00:25.415 --> 00:26.416
Where is Tokyo?

9
00:34.384 --> 00:35.385
Blue!

10
00:54.900 --> 00:55.901
Yi.

11
00:56.527 --> 00:57.700
Give me your sister's phone.

12
01:00.276 --> 01:01.277
From now on,

13
01:01.940 --> 01:04.740
you're not allowed to contact anyone.

14
01:07.044 --> 01:08.500
Dad, you can't do this.

15
01:12.600 --> 01:13.601
Tokyo.

16
01:17.200 --> 01:21.501
Don't you feel guilty that your mother died because of them?

17
01:22.796 --> 01:25.420
You told me Mom died in an accident.

18
01:26.556 --> 01:28.759
Dad, please. She's learned her lesson.

19
01:28.818 --> 01:30.060
And you, Yi.

20
01:30.545 --> 01:31.943
You're still taking her side?

21
01:35.860 --> 01:38.060
If you don't break up with that girl,

22
01:39.954 --> 01:42.140
I'll chain you up at home

23
01:43.052 --> 01:44.500
and never let you set foot outside again.

24
01:44.553 --> 01:46.200
Who I decide to date is none of your business.

25
01:46.220 --> 01:47.221
You're my daughter.

26
01:48.121 --> 01:49.660
You do what I tell you to do.

27
01:50.226 --> 01:51.227
Understand?

28
01:54.578 --> 01:55.660
That girl

29
01:56.964 --> 01:58.620
is the reason you've turned out like this.

30
01:58.983 --> 02:01.212
- See? - Dad, can you stop acting crazy?

31
02:02.754 --> 02:04.980
Everything that's happened is because of you.

32
02:05.324 --> 02:06.825
You're the one who picked a fight with that family

33
02:06.920 --> 02:08.860
just because you didn't get the port concession.

34
02:09.170 --> 02:11.500
If anyone has to die because of this, it'll be because of you.

35
02:11.930 --> 02:12.940
Dad! Dad!

36
02:17.474 --> 02:19.020
I'm not breaking up with Blue.

37
02:21.052 --> 02:23.953
We have nothing to do with your stupid feud.

38
02:23.963 --> 02:25.260
- Tokyo! - Dad!

39
02:26.500 --> 02:27.501
Dad!

40
02:29.140 --> 02:31.341
Dad, just let her go. She doesn't know anything. She's still a kid.

41
02:32.841 --> 02:33.842
Please, Dad.

42
02:36.519 --> 02:37.820
She's still a kid?

43
02:41.618 --> 02:43.100
Fine, if you said she's still a kid.

44
02:46.223 --> 02:48.130
Yi! Dad!

45
02:51.402 --> 02:52.403
Dad!

46
02:54.802 --> 02:56.803
Since your brother knew about it and kept quiet,

47
02:57.548 --> 02:59.004
he'll take the punishment for you.

48
03:01.415 --> 03:02.916
Dad! No!

49
03:04.400 --> 03:05.820
Dad!

50
03:23.060 --> 03:24.100
Give me your phone.

51
03:25.874 --> 03:26.875
No.

52
03:28.700 --> 03:29.876
You have no right to take it.

53
03:30.800 --> 03:31.870
It's mine.

54
03:34.450 --> 03:36.860
As long as you're still living off this family,

55
03:37.870 --> 03:39.420
you have to obey your parents.

56
03:43.340 --> 03:44.341
Mom!

57
03:47.800 --> 03:49.201
I just have a girlfriend.

58
03:50.301 --> 03:51.932
I haven't done anything wrong.

59
03:52.020 --> 03:54.200
- What is wrong with you and Dad? - Of course you've done something wrong.

60
03:57.602 --> 03:59.003
You still don't get it, do you?

61
03:59.841 --> 04:01.800
This isn't just about you anymore.

62
04:04.946 --> 04:07.647
You're causing trouble for everyone.

63
04:16.740 --> 04:18.841
I never raised you to be like this.

64
04:21.951 --> 04:24.952
You're selfish. You only think about yourself.

65
04:28.508 --> 04:31.209
Have you ever thought about anyone else involved in this?

66
04:52.276 --> 04:54.000
This is a matter of life and death.

67
04:55.967 --> 04:58.850
It's not just about two people being in love like you think.

68
05:22.500 --> 05:23.880
Forget about Tokyo.

69
05:27.562 --> 05:28.900
You don't get a choice.

70
05:39.620 --> 05:41.500
I've already arranged for you to move out of the dorm.

71
05:43.540 --> 05:44.541
From now on,

72
05:45.741 --> 05:47.354
you're moving back home.

73
07:42.500 --> 07:43.501
Dad.

74
07:44.770 --> 07:47.175
What are you going to ask for on your sister's behalf this time?

75
07:48.700 --> 07:49.701
Dad.

76
07:52.000 --> 07:54.139
She just wants to go to school in Bangkok.

77
07:57.284 --> 07:59.000
Can't we just let her go?

78
07:59.585 --> 08:00.900
Let her transfer to a school in Bangkok.

79
08:01.700 --> 08:03.701
Let her try being with that girl for a while.

80
08:03.800 --> 08:05.400
They'll break up eventually, Dad.

81
08:06.601 --> 08:08.502
It's just teenage love.

82
08:08.735 --> 08:10.060
We don't need to interfere.

83
08:11.736 --> 08:12.737
Love?

84
08:14.866 --> 08:15.900
Don't you remember

85
08:17.746 --> 08:20.147
someone once used love as an excuse

86
08:21.247 --> 08:23.660
and left us to pay the price for it?

87
08:26.351 --> 08:27.580
If you don't remember,

88
08:28.628 --> 08:29.660
I'll remind you

89
08:32.324 --> 08:35.050
who started all of this in the first place.

90
08:41.823 --> 08:43.251
But you're right about one thing.

91
08:46.554 --> 08:47.555
Your sister

92
08:48.700 --> 08:51.140
shouldn't have to be involved in this vendetta.

93
09:10.424 --> 09:12.500
Keep a close eye on her.

94
09:15.815 --> 09:17.830
Don't let her stray again.

95
09:19.400 --> 09:20.401
Understand?

96
09:39.431 --> 09:40.432
Tokyo.

97
09:41.200 --> 09:43.575
I've asked Jai and Pupay to pick you up outside the school.

98
09:44.642 --> 09:45.900
Stay close to those two.

99
09:59.391 --> 10:00.392
Hi.

100
10:12.970 --> 10:15.600
Hey, there's a new TikTok challenge. Let's do it.

101
10:36.200 --> 10:37.201
Sorry.

102
11:13.036 --> 11:14.060
Phakjira.

103
11:14.450 --> 11:17.451
It seems you've been causing more trouble than you realize lately.

104
11:20.732 --> 11:22.633
I want you to stay out of trouble.

105
11:23.733 --> 11:25.300
Anyone you shouldn't be involved with,

106
11:26.023 --> 11:27.324
you'd better stay away from them.

107
11:28.745 --> 11:30.060
And one more thing.

108
11:30.500 --> 11:33.660
If you disobey me, you might not graduate with your classmates.

109
11:36.063 --> 11:38.140
And that dream you've been chasing

110
11:39.738 --> 11:41.340
will remain nothing but a dream.

111
11:42.600 --> 11:43.601
Understand?

112
12:47.200 --> 12:48.268
Hello? What's up, Dad?

113
12:49.228 --> 12:50.229
I'm at school.

114
12:54.194 --> 12:55.565
Where the hell are you looking?

115
12:59.023 --> 13:02.300
Don't you think Pupay's been acting weird lately?

116
13:04.700 --> 13:05.701
Weird how?

117
13:09.295 --> 13:12.420
I don't know. She's been acting kind of shady.

118
13:14.650 --> 13:17.940
You think she's been telling her family about you?

119
13:25.660 --> 13:28.236
Okay, Tokyo, seriously.

120
13:28.780 --> 13:31.050
Since when does Pupay ever stick her nose into other people's business?

121
13:31.436 --> 13:34.500
I can gossip with the girl next door for an hour,

122
13:34.684 --> 13:36.540
and she just sits there listening without even caring.

123
13:37.140 --> 13:38.860
Why would she go tell her family about you?

124
13:40.108 --> 13:43.060
Yeah, maybe I'm overthinking it.

125
13:43.676 --> 13:45.060
But think about it.

126
13:45.756 --> 13:48.540
Her family's having money problems, and her dad owes my family money.

127
13:48.732 --> 13:50.660
Then all of a sudden, she shows up with a brand-new phone.

128
13:51.164 --> 13:52.340
How am I not supposed to be suspicious?

129
13:54.572 --> 13:57.580
Okay, seriously.

130
13:58.199 --> 14:01.100
Is there anyone besides your family who doesn't owe your family money?

131
14:01.620 --> 14:02.980
Even I do.

132
14:03.876 --> 14:06.100
So are you suspicious of me too?

133
14:10.399 --> 14:11.972
Exactly.

134
14:13.040 --> 14:14.041
See?

135
14:14.860 --> 14:16.450
Then couldn't it be anyone?

136
14:18.461 --> 14:20.150
- I don't know. - You really want to know, don't you?

137
14:21.900 --> 14:22.901
Here. Check it.

138
14:23.500 --> 14:26.150
Then you'll know whether I'm the one who went running to your dad.

139
14:29.300 --> 14:31.060
- Pupay. - Hey, you want to check my cloud too?

140
14:31.444 --> 14:32.660
Go ahead and check that too.

141
14:33.114 --> 14:35.020
Then maybe you'll finally stop wondering if it was me.

142
14:36.500 --> 14:39.921
- It's not what you think. - If you really saw me as your friend from the start,

143
14:40.540 --> 14:41.800
why would you suspect me in the first place?

144
14:46.522 --> 14:48.460
- Pupay! - Pupay!

145
14:48.506 --> 14:49.507
Pupay, wait.

146
14:50.800 --> 14:51.801
Pupay!

147
14:52.047 --> 14:54.520
- Pupay, wait! - Wait for Tokyo.

148
14:57.311 --> 14:58.312
Hey.

149
14:58.719 --> 15:00.820
- I'm sorry. - What's the point of apologizing now?

150
15:03.402 --> 15:05.640
Deep down, you think I'm just like all your other friends, don't you?

151
15:07.690 --> 15:08.891
You think I'm only friends with you because of your money,

152
15:08.900 --> 15:10.460
because of your family, because of who your dad is, right?

153
15:12.180 --> 15:13.500
Well, let me tell you something.

154
15:13.791 --> 15:16.000
I've never even cared who the hell your dad is.

155
15:18.108 --> 15:19.860
I just like being with you. I like hanging out with you guys.

156
15:19.880 --> 15:21.600
Because you never cared that I was poor,

157
15:21.660 --> 15:22.661
unlike what everyone else says about me.

158
15:25.826 --> 15:27.420
But if being friends with me makes you uncomfortable

159
15:27.440 --> 15:28.860
or you don't feel okay being friends with me anymore,

160
15:29.980 --> 15:31.360
then we just don't have to be friends. That's it.

161
15:41.815 --> 15:44.231
It's okay. She's probably still mad.

162
15:44.322 --> 15:45.640
Just give her some space for now.

163
15:46.071 --> 15:48.860
You can talk to her once she's calmed down.

164
15:59.023 --> 16:00.200
You two.

165
16:01.978 --> 16:02.979
Come here.

166
16:10.450 --> 16:12.340
From now on, you're both blacklisted.

167
16:13.108 --> 16:15.220
You're not allowed to meet in the library anymore.

168
16:18.109 --> 16:19.110
Get out.

169
16:37.762 --> 16:40.560
Tokyo, Miss Vee wants to see you in her office.

170
16:40.911 --> 16:42.800
She said you haven't turned in all your club assignments.

171
16:45.090 --> 16:46.091
The club?

172
16:46.716 --> 16:47.717
What club?

173
16:49.980 --> 16:51.340
She called Blue in too.

174
16:51.981 --> 16:54.020
I think she wants to talk about you moving out of the dorm.

175
16:59.596 --> 17:02.860
You haven't turned in all your Environmental Club reports, Tokyo.

176
17:04.863 --> 17:06.300
Environmental Club?

177
17:08.527 --> 17:11.528
No, I'm in the Literature Club.

178
17:14.020 --> 17:15.140
Oh, really?

179
17:17.621 --> 17:19.422
Then your name must've been added by mistake.

180
17:19.622 --> 17:22.500
But that's okay. Write the report now and hand it in to me

181
17:22.591 --> 17:23.592
so you can pass.

182
17:25.500 --> 17:27.200
And you, Phakjira.

183
17:27.418 --> 17:29.231
Even though you've already moved out of the dorm,

184
17:29.300 --> 17:31.301
you left your room in a terrible mess.

185
17:32.000 --> 17:34.301
So sit right next to her and write an apology letter.

186
17:36.100 --> 17:37.101
Okay.

187
17:38.210 --> 17:41.143
You two stay here and finish your work.

188
17:41.724 --> 17:42.725
I'll be back.

189
18:13.050 --> 18:14.051
How are you doing?

190
18:15.519 --> 18:17.400
I'm okay. What about you?

191
18:18.074 --> 18:19.901
Yeah, I'm fine.

192
18:23.492 --> 18:27.493
I think Miss Vee might be the only teacher in this school

193
18:28.100 --> 18:29.201
who's actually on our side.

194
18:39.092 --> 18:40.093
But yesterday,

195
18:41.450 --> 18:43.020
my dad was furious.

196
18:45.071 --> 18:48.260
He brought up my mom's death

197
18:50.026 --> 18:53.140
and said it had something to do with the Monchaitrakul family.

198
18:58.378 --> 19:00.620
Do you know anything about that?

199
19:07.871 --> 19:09.100
I've never heard anything about it.

200
19:13.580 --> 19:16.581
I thought Uncle Wirat's death

201
19:16.900 --> 19:18.901
was what started this whole stupid feud.

202
19:20.495 --> 19:21.820
So your mom was involved too?

203
19:24.847 --> 19:28.580
I think my dad's always tried to avoid talking about my mom.

204
19:29.948 --> 19:33.460
But he was so angry last night that he let it slip.

205
19:36.439 --> 19:39.700
I think if we want to put an end to all this,

206
19:40.440 --> 19:42.401
we might have to find the answers together

207
19:43.741 --> 19:44.980
and figure out how it all started.

208
19:46.807 --> 19:47.808
Yeah.

209
20:57.020 --> 20:58.021
Anything?

210
21:07.794 --> 21:08.795
Here.

211
21:09.596 --> 21:11.380
Here it is. The article about my mom.

212
21:12.794 --> 21:14.900
- [Woman Killed in Car Fire, Child Miraculously Survives] - My dad and brothers always told me

213
21:15.834 --> 21:17.900
that my mom died in a car fire.

214
21:24.380 --> 21:26.180
This one must be about Pakkard's dad.

215
21:26.620 --> 21:28.980
Businessman Named Wirat Brutally Killed in Robbery.

216
21:29.158 --> 21:31.230
Why does everything keep happening in cars? Look at this.

217
21:34.103 --> 21:35.746
It's just like my dad told me.

218
21:37.250 --> 21:38.660
As soon as Uncle Wirat died,

219
21:41.042 --> 21:42.943
Kongpurim got the concession.

220
21:59.394 --> 22:01.000
It can't be a coincidence

221
22:02.615 --> 22:04.116
that all these events are connected, right?

222
22:07.380 --> 22:08.381
No.

223
22:10.123 --> 22:11.924
But if we ask anyone about this,

224
22:13.620 --> 22:15.321
I doubt they'll tell us the truth.

225
22:26.964 --> 22:27.965
But there's one person

226
22:29.578 --> 22:30.740
who can't lie to us.

227
22:52.170 --> 22:53.171
Amen.

228
23:01.218 --> 23:03.060
Father, there's something we'd like to ask you.

229
23:04.332 --> 23:05.800
We'd like you to answer us, Father.

230
23:07.756 --> 23:09.140
If I can answer, I will.

231
23:18.618 --> 23:20.120
Seventeen years ago,

232
23:22.756 --> 23:24.420
what happened to my mother?

233
23:28.884 --> 23:30.300
Please don't lie to us, Father.

234
23:33.226 --> 23:34.460
God is listening.

235
23:38.068 --> 23:39.500
Did my mother's death

236
23:40.906 --> 23:42.660
have something to do with Mr. Wirat?

237
23:45.140 --> 23:47.655
Yes. But I can't tell you everything.

238
23:47.788 --> 23:48.789
I wasn't there.

239
23:49.495 --> 23:53.383
But what I can tell you is that the feud between the two families

240
23:53.890 --> 23:54.891
started with Wirat

241
23:57.900 --> 24:00.100
and Sirin, your mother.

242
24:12.743 --> 24:14.460
But there's no way my mother

243
24:14.770 --> 24:17.575
would've held a grudge against anyone or hurt anyone, right?

244
24:18.194 --> 24:20.576
It wasn't hatred that started it all.

245
24:38.007 --> 24:39.008
Tokyo.

246
24:40.828 --> 24:41.829
It's time to go home.

247
24:45.829 --> 24:48.550
You should take your friend home too.

248
24:48.830 --> 24:50.000
Before anyone sees you.

249
24:59.322 --> 25:00.323
Go.

250
25:09.970 --> 25:11.340
I don't think it's broken.

251
25:12.268 --> 25:15.500
Oh, really? I wasn't sure.

252
25:15.682 --> 25:16.683
I saw it flickering.

253
25:17.340 --> 25:18.620
The bulb might be going out.

254
25:28.372 --> 25:30.500
How long have you worked here, Auntie Poo?

255
25:31.626 --> 25:32.780
Since before Blue was born.

256
25:33.306 --> 25:36.068
Wow, so

257
25:36.420 --> 25:38.900
you were already here when Uncle Wirat was still alive, right?

258
25:39.836 --> 25:40.837
Yes, I was.

259
25:48.252 --> 25:49.253
So...

260
25:51.127 --> 25:52.700
how did Uncle Wirat die?

261
25:57.878 --> 25:58.879
You're better off not knowing.

262
26:00.279 --> 26:02.980
Please, Uncle Phu. I really need to know.

263
26:03.516 --> 26:05.517
No one in this family will tell me anything.

264
26:06.436 --> 26:08.460
But I trust that you won't keep it from me.

265
26:14.380 --> 26:15.381
Back then,

266
26:16.954 --> 26:18.660
there was a lot of chaos in town.

267
26:19.612 --> 26:21.460
It was all because of the fight over the port concession.

268
26:22.500 --> 26:23.501
That family

269
26:24.124 --> 26:26.000
made the first move and killed Mr. Wirat.

270
26:27.825 --> 26:29.220
They shot him dead

271
26:30.596 --> 26:33.640
and staged it as a robbery to cover their tracks.

272
26:36.020 --> 26:37.060
They dared to do it

273
26:37.700 --> 26:40.660
because Monchaitrakul was about to win the province's biggest port concession.

274
26:40.701 --> 26:42.002
[Kongpurim Secures Port Concession for Decades]

275
26:42.020 --> 26:43.660
No one dared go up against that family.

276
26:45.423 --> 26:47.444
That's why your father's held onto this grudge all these years.

277
26:55.458 --> 26:57.000
Try to understand your father, Blue.

278
26:58.140 --> 26:59.180
If it were you,

279
26:59.394 --> 27:01.900
and your brother had been murdered, you'd be angry too, wouldn't you?

280
27:14.900 --> 27:18.001
You two...

281
27:18.948 --> 27:19.949
I'm begging you.

282
27:20.868 --> 27:22.600
Can't you just be kids?

283
27:24.047 --> 27:25.945
Stay out of the adults' feud.

284
27:41.276 --> 27:42.277
Hey.

285
27:43.300 --> 27:46.420
Hey, I'm fine.

286
27:48.001 --> 27:49.402
I don't want to dwell on this either.

287
27:51.639 --> 27:52.660
The past is the past.

288
28:45.633 --> 28:47.500
- What's this? - Money.

289
28:47.746 --> 28:48.847
Did your brain stop working?

290
28:50.580 --> 28:51.581
I know what it is.

291
28:54.000 --> 28:55.200
Where did you get it?

292
28:57.200 --> 29:00.100
It's mine. My savings.

293
29:01.700 --> 29:04.420
I think you and your girlfriend should get out of this town as soon as you can.

294
29:06.546 --> 29:09.420
I have a feeling our family and theirs are going to clash sooner or later.

295
29:12.071 --> 29:13.740
And I don't want you getting caught up in this because of me again.

296
29:15.618 --> 29:18.900
It's not because of you. It's because of Dad.

297
29:20.076 --> 29:21.077
It is because of me.

298
29:22.177 --> 29:24.220
Just tell me when you and your girlfriend are leaving.

299
29:24.674 --> 29:26.700
The sooner, the better. Got it?

300
29:31.405 --> 29:34.540
But if Dad finds out, he'll kill you, Yi.

301
29:35.290 --> 29:36.420
Look at what he did to you the other day.

302
29:37.580 --> 29:38.900
That's probably the worst he'll do.

303
29:39.380 --> 29:40.460
At most, I'll be covered in poop.

304
29:40.901 --> 29:42.980
I've still got the eldest-son card to play.

305
29:43.500 --> 29:44.750
Dad won't let me die.

306
29:45.600 --> 29:47.700
I still have to carry on the Kongpurim family line.

307
29:49.111 --> 29:50.220
Besides, I think

308
29:52.092 --> 29:53.720
this scar actually looks pretty cool.

309
29:54.093 --> 29:55.094
Right?

310
29:57.724 --> 29:59.125
Ow! Ow!

311
29:59.596 --> 30:01.100
That hurts! What are you doing?

312
30:01.735 --> 30:03.300
Who told you to joke about that?

313
30:06.535 --> 30:07.830
Come here. Give me a hug.

314
30:11.432 --> 30:13.540
- You smell like poop. - Ew, snot!

315
30:14.439 --> 30:15.540
I don't want to hug you anymore.

316
30:16.335 --> 30:17.336
Gross.

317
30:43.802 --> 30:44.803
Please help me out, sir.

318
30:45.620 --> 30:47.140
Whatever you want,

319
30:47.559 --> 30:49.220
I'll make it worth your while.

320
30:55.156 --> 30:56.350
All right, I'll call you back.

321
30:58.260 --> 31:00.940
Boss, I managed to recover the corrupted CCTV footage.

322
31:17.746 --> 31:19.080
- [Everything's going according to plan.] - Should we wait for the police?

323
31:24.660 --> 31:26.900
- [Temporarily Closed for Renovation] - Yeah, yeah.

324
31:27.100 --> 31:29.060
- [Do Not Enter Without Permission] - Go all out.

325
31:31.100 --> 31:32.101
Come on, give it everything you've got!

326
31:47.300 --> 31:48.401
Is something wrong, Boss?

327
31:55.500 --> 31:57.620
Your daughter needs regular dialysis, doesn't she?

328
31:59.300 --> 32:00.620
How much does it cost a month?

329
32:03.639 --> 32:05.140
I'm not like the Kongpurims.

330
32:05.740 --> 32:07.900
I don't go around killing people.

331
32:08.940 --> 32:09.941
I'm a businessman.

332
32:10.500 --> 32:13.540
Businessmen negotiate with money.

333
32:16.225 --> 32:18.460
I'll pay off all her hospital bills,

334
32:19.485 --> 32:21.600
and I'll pay for your daughter's education too.

335
32:23.260 --> 32:26.020
All you have to do is testify against the Kongpurims.

336
32:27.076 --> 32:28.077
Deal?

337
32:47.031 --> 32:48.450
Mr. Wiboon, are you sure

338
32:49.052 --> 32:51.060
you have evidence that the Kongpurims were behind it?

339
32:55.751 --> 32:56.752
I'm sure.

340
32:57.767 --> 32:59.180
Inspector, please give me a moment.

341
32:59.900 --> 33:01.300
My witness is on his way.

342
33:14.738 --> 33:16.700
Boss, the witness has been assassinated.

343
33:25.400 --> 33:27.901
[Chanthabun Provincial Police Station]

344
33:34.600 --> 33:35.960
Don't do anything.

345
33:37.000 --> 33:38.420
Our time is almost here.

346
33:59.780 --> 34:00.940
Why are you giving this to me?

347
34:03.346 --> 34:06.258
Well, I don't know who else to give it to.

348
34:08.866 --> 34:10.140
I probably won't be taking it with me.

349
34:13.580 --> 34:14.620
So you're really going through with it?

350
34:16.631 --> 34:18.540
I thought you were just making up some crazy plan for fun.

351
34:21.575 --> 34:22.576
I'm not joking.

352
34:23.537 --> 34:24.538
I'm serious.

353
34:27.396 --> 34:29.800
We probably can't meet at the library anymore.

354
34:30.541 --> 34:31.542
So...

355
34:32.459 --> 34:33.540
how about we meet here instead?

356
34:35.638 --> 34:37.700
Tokyo and I have been thinking about this for a while.

357
34:40.200 --> 34:43.339
We're going to run away together.

358
34:45.628 --> 34:47.629
We won't have to keep hiding anymore.

359
34:48.300 --> 34:50.400
We'll leave as soon as our final exams are over.

360
34:50.890 --> 34:53.660
And Yi really knows about this, right?

361
34:55.600 --> 34:56.601
Yeah.

362
34:57.812 --> 34:59.400
He already promised Tokyo he'd help us.

363
35:02.345 --> 35:03.524
I put a prepaid SIM in it for you.

364
35:05.551 --> 35:06.552
Thank you.

365
35:09.349 --> 35:12.092
Yi, it's tomorrow.

366
35:24.650 --> 35:27.400
You've got me. What are you scared of?

367
35:32.292 --> 35:34.100
And answer your phone when I call, okay?

368
35:34.746 --> 35:36.820
Don't run away from home and start acting like some wild kid.

369
35:38.825 --> 35:41.220
I'll answer. I know.

370
35:46.372 --> 35:47.580
After this,

371
35:48.474 --> 35:50.185
we probably won't get to see each other very often.

372
36:00.748 --> 36:01.749
Yeah.

373
36:03.500 --> 36:04.501
I will send you off, don't worry.

374
36:09.463 --> 36:11.164
Thanks.

375
36:16.567 --> 36:17.860
You're gonna miss me, right?

376
36:20.439 --> 36:21.540
Of course I am.

377
36:26.802 --> 36:27.940
Are you sure you can handle yourself?

378
36:33.905 --> 36:34.906
I'll be fine.

379
37:28.900 --> 37:29.901
Jai.

380
37:31.101 --> 37:33.140
Just stop running away.

381
37:33.249 --> 37:36.044
You know you can never escape the Kongpurims.

382
37:38.236 --> 37:39.237
What about you?

383
37:43.135 --> 37:44.840
Have you been spying on me for my family?

384
37:46.740 --> 37:48.141
Can you not say that?

385
37:48.941 --> 37:52.740
You know how much my life depends on your family.

386
37:53.471 --> 37:56.172
My family still owes your dad money.

387
37:57.535 --> 37:59.748
And then there's the school singer thing.

388
38:00.063 --> 38:01.620
If the teachers weren't trying to stay on your good side,

389
38:01.700 --> 38:03.181
do you think I'd even get to perform onstage?

390
38:05.119 --> 38:08.180
If I don't become a singer, if I don't make it big,

391
38:08.420 --> 38:09.820
how am I ever gonna be rich like you?

392
38:09.840 --> 38:11.580
Can you just stop talking?

393
38:13.914 --> 38:16.540
Fine. I'll stop.

394
38:18.543 --> 38:21.060
But if I do, will you come home with me?

395
38:33.300 --> 38:34.940
This guy grabbed my boobs!

396
38:34.960 --> 38:37.400
Hey, hey! Watch what you're saying. I didn't do anything!

397
39:04.300 --> 39:05.301
Are you okay?

398
39:13.466 --> 39:14.860
Jai betrayed us.

399
39:18.400 --> 39:19.701
She's been spying on us for my family.

400
39:26.500 --> 39:27.740
It's okay.

401
39:28.954 --> 39:30.660
Maybe your dad forced her to do it.

402
39:36.303 --> 39:37.304
No.

403
39:40.000 --> 39:41.300
She chose to do it herself.

404
39:57.159 --> 39:58.260
I don't even know anymore

405
39:59.324 --> 40:01.300
if she ever really wanted

406
40:04.242 --> 40:06.140
to be my friend all this time.

407
40:19.015 --> 40:21.084
There's no point trying to figure that out right now.

408
40:23.016 --> 40:26.740
Once we get out of here, we can find the answer together, okay?

409
40:35.400 --> 40:36.900
But I don't know

410
40:38.362 --> 40:42.000
if I'll ever want to believe anything she says again.

411
40:52.924 --> 40:54.200
It's almost nine.

412
40:58.516 --> 41:00.000
Yi should be here soon.

413
41:22.600 --> 41:24.300
[Pakkard: Those two changed the plan.]

414
41:24.410 --> 41:25.700
[Meet under the railway bridge at the same time.]

415
41:42.657 --> 41:45.060
I can't even tell what's tears and what's rain anymore.

416
42:00.804 --> 42:02.500
But Yi's really coming, right?

417
42:10.700 --> 42:12.400
Yi would never break his promise to us.

418
42:24.132 --> 42:25.133
Where are those two?

419
42:34.308 --> 42:35.309
Huh?

420
42:38.876 --> 42:40.100
How did my dad die?

421
43:01.068 --> 43:02.069
Hello, Yi?

422
43:04.865 --> 43:05.980
Where's my sister?

423
43:07.100 --> 43:09.701
What the hell, Pakkard? What's wrong with you?

424
43:10.200 --> 43:12.150
Tell me how my dad died.

425
43:13.820 --> 43:14.821
What about Dad?

426
43:27.700 --> 43:28.701
Hurry, get inside.

427
43:30.119 --> 43:32.000
- What about you? - We'll figure that out later.

428
43:34.400 --> 43:35.401
Go!

429
44:43.418 --> 44:44.830
Why the hell are you doing this?

430
44:50.546 --> 44:51.820
How did my dad die?

431
44:54.994 --> 44:56.420
What? What the hell are you talking about?

432
45:00.300 --> 45:01.301
Where's my sister?

433
45:02.600 --> 45:05.020
What the hell is wrong with you, Pakkard?

434
45:05.500 --> 45:07.340
Tell me how my dad died.

435
45:07.501 --> 45:09.600
You're the one who killed my dad, aren't you?

436
45:11.700 --> 45:12.820
[Businessman named Wirat Brutally Killed in Robbery Inside Luxury Car]

437
45:17.871 --> 45:19.062
Are you gonna tell me now?

438
45:25.700 --> 45:26.701
Pakkard.

439
45:28.000 --> 45:29.001
Calm down.

440
45:29.988 --> 45:31.580
Just calm down and listen to me.

441
45:32.743 --> 45:34.400
I don't know what you heard,

442
45:37.015 --> 45:38.250
but whatever you heard isn't true.

443
45:38.279 --> 45:40.050
Your family's the one who's been lying to me.

444
45:40.359 --> 45:43.060
All of you are the reason my life turned out like this.

445
45:43.226 --> 45:45.060
No, no. Calm down.

446
45:45.227 --> 45:46.228
Put the gun down.

447
45:46.980 --> 45:47.981
Just calm down.

448
45:48.820 --> 45:50.180
What the fuck? Are you really gonna kill me?

449
45:50.230 --> 45:51.660
Go blame your father.

450
45:51.690 --> 45:54.020
I'm telling you, the reason your life turned out like this is because of him.

451
46:42.348 --> 46:43.700
Why are you doing this?

452
47:14.084 --> 47:16.500
- [Next Episode Preview] - Our family is looking for Pakkard right now.

453
47:16.711 --> 47:19.630
My parents have taken Pakkard to the border.

454
47:20.340 --> 47:22.200
So you helped Pakkard escape too?

455
47:22.741 --> 47:25.620
Do you still believe in your pure, innocent love?

456
47:25.942 --> 47:27.420
Or do you think your love

457
47:27.756 --> 47:30.420
can wash away your mother's blood from the past?

458
47:32.060 --> 47:34.460
Everything has already been decided.

459
47:34.604 --> 47:36.580
You just have to play your part.
